            <ArticleTitle>[Neuro-ophthalmologic relations in cervical syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>53-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this article are reported three cases with ocular disturbances manifested by trophic keratitis, hypoesthesia of cornea and descemet precipitates. These disturbances have a connection with phenomenon caused by circulatory insufficiency within the territory of the vertebral artery, with involvement of the bulbo-protuberantial nuclei. The clinical manifestations are vestibular and visual disturbances, occipital headaches which means that the cervical sympathetic nerve was affected.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
